<title>NETHERLANDS: Dollar lifts Royal Dutch shares to new highs.</title>
<headline>Dollar lifts Royal Dutch shares to new highs.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>A firmer dollar lifted shares of Royal Dutch Petroleum Co to new highs for the year on Monday.</p>
<p>At 0930 GMT Royal Dutch shares were 4.30 guilders firmer at 295.10 after erlier touching a high of 296.00.</p>
<p>Dealers said the firmer dollar was the main reason for the higher share price, noting that Royal Dutch had actually closed lower in New York on Monday while other U.S. oil stocks were little changed despite firmer oil prices.</p>
<p>The dollar was trading above 1.75 guilders today after trading around 1.72 guilders for most of Monday.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
